WEBVTT

00:02.670 --> 00:03.560
Wow.

00:03.560 --> 00:05.440
They're always so cool.

00:05.440 --> 00:07.620
You think they're dating?

00:07.620 --> 00:10.250
I hate to admit it, 
but they make a great couple.

00:12.180 --> 00:13.840
Can't disagree with that.

00:14.570 --> 00:15.620
They're amazing.

00:17.760 --> 00:21.380
The student council's moment 
of truth has finally come.

00:21.690 --> 00:25.130
We'll get the school regulations amended, 
 fulfilling our promise to the student body.

00:21.700 --> 00:25.120
<b>Student Council President
Suzune Inukami</b>

00:21.700 --> 00:25.120
<b>Student Council President
Suzune Inukami</b>

00:25.120 --> 00:31.050
<b>Student Council Vice President
Kazuki Ryusen</b>

00:25.120 --> 00:31.050
<b>Student Council Vice President
Kazuki Ryusen</b>

00:25.380 --> 00:27.090
Yes, Inukami-senpai.

00:27.090 --> 00:30.330
I've got the documents we need 
to make a compelling argument.

00:31.620 --> 00:36.230
<i>Some people in this world are 
always the center of attention.</i>

00:36.850 --> 00:38.260
See you later, Usato.

00:38.260 --> 00:39.300
Later.

00:39.300 --> 00:40.880
See you tomorrow.

00:41.960 --> 00:44.000
<i>I'm the opposite.</i>

00:41.970 --> 00:47.400
<b>Ordinary Student
Ken Usato</b>

00:41.970 --> 00:47.400
<b>Ordinary Student
Ken Usato</b>

00:44.000 --> 00:47.060
<i>I'm a forgettable, run-of-the-mill 
high school student.</i>

00:48.000 --> 00:51.460
<i>Even if something out of the 
ordinary happens to me,</i>

00:54.490 --> 00:56.530
<i>it's rarely more exciting than this.</i>

00:57.950 --> 01:00.410
Grow big and strong!

01:00.410 --> 01:04.140
And feel free to pay me back 
if you ever feel like it.

01:04.570 --> 01:05.630
Yeah, right.

01:06.450 --> 01:10.240
<i>But in my heart, I'm always hoping...</i>

01:10.760 --> 01:15.340
<i>for an extraordinary and fantastical life.</i>

01:16.090 --> 01:19.890
<b>#1 Dragged into Another World!</b>

01:20.340 --> 01:21.530
It's not here.

01:22.450 --> 01:26.720
<i>Someone must've taken it. 
That's a stroke of bad luck.</i>

01:32.620 --> 01:34.690
<i>No, I couldn't do that.</i>

01:34.690 --> 01:38.500
<i>I'd be screwing over the owner, 
and I don't want any trouble.</i>

01:42.370 --> 01:45.240
If only I could use magic.

01:49.510 --> 01:51.590
Guess I'll wait a while.

01:54.500 --> 01:55.830
It's not stopping!

01:55.830 --> 01:56.760
Oh?

01:57.590 --> 02:00.260
What are you doing?

02:00.260 --> 02:00.970
What?

02:00.970 --> 02:03.420
Could it be that you don't have an umbrella?

02:03.420 --> 02:06.650
Well, uh... yes.

02:06.650 --> 02:07.940
I see.

02:08.230 --> 02:12.110
But all students are required to leave soon.

02:12.110 --> 02:16.160
Y-You're right. I'll head home right away.

02:16.160 --> 02:17.840
Wait.

02:17.840 --> 02:21.800
Sending a student home in the rain would 
damage the student council's dignity.

02:21.800 --> 02:23.090
In that case, Senpai,

02:23.540 --> 02:26.360
I'll lend Usato-kun my spare umbrella.

02:26.360 --> 02:27.290
What?

02:27.290 --> 02:30.030
Kazuki-kun, you know him?

02:30.030 --> 02:31.960
Yes. We're classmates.

02:31.960 --> 02:34.350
<i>We've never spoken before,</i>

02:34.350 --> 02:36.630
<i>but he knows my name.</i>

02:36.630 --> 02:38.810
Usato-kun, use this.

02:39.240 --> 02:44.440
<i>I guess Kazuki Ryusen 
is actually a nice guy after all.</i>

02:46.980 --> 02:49.150
Th-Thank you, Ryusen-kun.

02:49.150 --> 02:52.810
No need to be so formal. 
We're classmates, after all.

02:52.810 --> 02:55.590
I'll call you, uh...

02:56.390 --> 02:58.870
Usato? No, Ken?

02:59.390 --> 03:00.900
Usato is fine.

03:01.220 --> 03:03.690
I like being called that.

03:03.690 --> 03:05.290
Got it, Usato.

03:05.290 --> 03:07.950
I'll call you Usato-kun as well.

03:08.310 --> 03:09.870
Is that all right, Usato-kun?

03:09.870 --> 03:10.650
Huh?

03:11.160 --> 03:13.070
Th-That's fine.

03:13.070 --> 03:15.660
In that case, Usato, 
let's head home together.

03:15.660 --> 03:18.850
Yes, let's. It must be fate that we met.

03:19.170 --> 03:23.250
<i>I've suddenly hit a "walking home with two 
of the most popular kids at school" event?</i>

03:23.910 --> 03:26.150
The entire school will be jealous.

03:26.150 --> 03:27.190
What?

03:27.190 --> 03:29.860
Oh, nothing.

03:30.860 --> 03:35.680
Honestly, Kazuki, I didn't expect 
you to be this friendly.

03:35.680 --> 03:37.690
What? Why?

03:37.690 --> 03:41.370
Because I've only ever seen you 
talking to the girls in our class.

03:41.370 --> 03:44.640
I'm just engaging with them because 
they start conversations with me.

03:45.530 --> 03:50.350
In other words, the other 
boys won't talk to you.

03:50.350 --> 03:51.830
S-Senpai!

03:52.180 --> 03:53.280
Sorry.

03:53.600 --> 03:59.460
I actually thought Inukami-senpai 
was even less approachable.

03:59.460 --> 04:01.290
What? How could you?

04:01.290 --> 04:03.770
I'm an ordinary high school third-year.

04:03.770 --> 04:05.790
You're hardly ordinary.

04:06.060 --> 04:09.020
You're top of your class in all 
subjects and great at all sports.

04:09.020 --> 04:10.960
To top it off, you're 
beautiful inside and out.

04:11.260 --> 04:13.810
You should view yourself more objectively.

04:14.290 --> 04:16.930
You're being unusually 
hard on me, Kazuki-kun.

04:17.230 --> 04:19.190
I'm just getting you back for earlier.

04:20.270 --> 04:23.610
So, are you two dating?

04:23.920 --> 04:24.810
What?

04:24.810 --> 04:28.740
What? Uh, that's what everyone says...

04:28.740 --> 04:31.590
Obviously we're not dating.

04:31.590 --> 04:32.940
That's right.

04:32.940 --> 04:37.160
We simply spend a lot of time together 
because we're both on the student council.

04:37.160 --> 04:38.550
You're kidding, right?

04:38.550 --> 04:40.500
Why would we lie about that?

04:40.500 --> 04:44.050
I know a lot of people think we're dating,

04:44.050 --> 04:49.060
but you're the first one who's 
asked us directly, Usato-kun.

04:49.060 --> 04:50.300
S-Sorry.

04:51.090 --> 04:52.670
It's a compliment.

04:52.670 --> 04:55.270
It's way better than whispering 
about it behind our backs.

05:00.510 --> 05:02.820
Can I ask you something, too?

05:03.790 --> 05:07.890
Usato-kun, have you thought about 
what you'll do after high school?

05:08.280 --> 05:11.540
What? Not yet, I guess.

05:11.540 --> 05:14.100
I see. Not yet, huh?

05:15.890 --> 05:19.240
Senpai, you asked me that question, too.

05:19.240 --> 05:22.800
I'm just curious about 
other people's answers.

05:23.340 --> 05:25.980
Because I don't have any plans myself.

05:26.470 --> 05:29.730
What? Inukami-senpai, you haven't 
decided what you'll do after graduation?

05:29.730 --> 05:32.140
You're a third-year. That can't be good.

05:32.970 --> 05:34.660
You're not wrong.

05:35.060 --> 05:38.170
I still haven't found what I want to do.

05:38.680 --> 05:41.890
I immediately complete 
any goal I set for myself.

05:42.290 --> 05:44.310
I-I see.

05:44.310 --> 05:48.750
<i>So that's what competent people worry about. 
Not that I'd have any idea.</i>

05:48.990 --> 05:55.070
Sometimes I feel like this 
isn't where I belong.

05:56.240 --> 05:58.680
<i>Senpai and I are nothing alike,</i>

05:58.680 --> 06:01.590
<i>but I think I understand that feeling.</i>

06:09.840 --> 06:12.390
What's that sound?

06:12.390 --> 06:13.950
Huh? What's the matter?

06:14.300 --> 06:17.000
Usato, did you hear something just now?

06:17.000 --> 06:18.610
Like bells ringing.

06:18.610 --> 06:21.220
No, I didn't hear anything.

06:24.520 --> 06:26.490
I hear it.

06:26.930 --> 06:28.660
It's getting louder.

06:28.980 --> 06:31.320
What is this? Where's it coming from?

06:31.320 --> 06:33.240
I really don't hear anything.

06:33.720 --> 06:34.670
Are you okay?

06:42.580 --> 06:44.360
A magic circle?

06:44.660 --> 06:47.470
What is this? Did we wander 
into a film shoot?

06:47.470 --> 06:49.570
Is this a gate to another world?

06:49.570 --> 06:51.350
What are you talking about?

06:51.350 --> 06:52.690
Usato-kun.

06:53.340 --> 06:58.940
Do you think we'll find magic and 
monsters and heroes in this other world?

06:59.580 --> 07:00.580
What?

07:00.580 --> 07:03.920
<i>Does Inukami-senpai like that kind of thing?</i>

07:03.920 --> 07:05.620
<i>I can worry about that later!</i>

07:13.610 --> 07:16.370
Usato. Hey, Usato.

07:24.970 --> 07:25.940
What?

07:25.940 --> 07:27.490
Are you okay, Usato?

07:28.060 --> 07:29.610
Y-Yeah.

07:30.500 --> 07:33.550
Kazuki, where are we?

07:33.890 --> 07:36.570
Wh-Who are they?

07:36.570 --> 07:37.840
I don't know.

07:37.840 --> 07:40.600
Senpai just woke me up, too.

07:40.600 --> 07:42.690
Oh, right. Where is she?

07:43.450 --> 07:44.300
What?

07:44.300 --> 07:47.870
Usato-kun, you were right.

07:48.440 --> 07:51.020
This place is probably...

07:51.020 --> 07:52.920
<i>She's excited!</i>

07:53.170 --> 07:56.060
Looks like you're all awake.

07:56.630 --> 08:00.200
I'm sure suddenly coming here 
has left you bewildered—

08:00.200 --> 08:03.010
Who are you? What did you do to us?

08:03.320 --> 08:06.050
How dare you disrespect 
His Majesty King Lloyd?

08:06.050 --> 08:07.580
Enough.

08:08.190 --> 08:12.160
Forgive me. I understand your confusion.

08:12.160 --> 08:16.170
But please hear what I have to say.

08:16.810 --> 08:22.030
I am Lloyd Vulgast Llinger, King of Llinger.

08:24.150 --> 08:25.490
A king?

08:26.030 --> 08:27.290
A real king!

08:27.820 --> 08:29.940
Uh, Senpai...

08:29.940 --> 08:32.030
Allow me to be direct.

08:32.030 --> 08:35.900
We summoned you to the Llinger Kingdom...

08:36.930 --> 08:38.350
to serve as heroes.

08:38.350 --> 08:39.790
What? Heroes?

08:39.790 --> 08:41.200
Heck yes!

08:41.200 --> 08:44.610
<i>Please stop ruining my image of you!</i>

08:44.610 --> 08:50.080
Two years ago, we were attacked 
by this world's king of demons.

08:50.370 --> 08:52.580
King of demons?

08:52.580 --> 08:54.170
A-A demon lord?!

08:54.170 --> 08:58.010
<i>They're having a serious conversation! 
Restrain yourself!</i>

08:58.010 --> 09:03.420
Indeed. He invaded our nation with an army.

09:03.670 --> 09:10.020
We managed to drive them off, but the
 Demon Lord's army has been expanding its power.

09:10.020 --> 09:12.530
There's no telling what will happen next time.

09:12.870 --> 09:15.160
So as a last resort, we called forth
 accomplished individuals

09:15.160 --> 09:20.360
from another world who can confront 
the Demon Lord, using a forbidden ritual

09:20.360 --> 09:22.780
known as Hero Summoning.

09:23.700 --> 09:25.430
Forbidden! Summoning!

09:25.430 --> 09:26.710
You can't be serious!

09:28.120 --> 09:30.430
I don't care about heroes or demon lords.

09:30.430 --> 09:32.760
How dare you bring us here 
without our consent?

09:32.760 --> 09:36.010
Send us back to our own world this instant!

09:36.010 --> 09:38.080
I'm sorry, but that is simply not possible.

09:38.080 --> 09:41.200
The Hero Summoning only 
works in one direction.

09:41.200 --> 09:45.180
It can bring people here, 
but it cannot send them back.

09:45.180 --> 09:47.650
Then what's going to happen to us?

09:47.650 --> 09:49.510
I have a family back home.

09:49.510 --> 09:51.610
So do Senpai and Usato.

09:51.610 --> 09:56.140
I am sorry, but we are desperate.

09:56.140 --> 09:58.070
You can't expect me to accept—

10:02.500 --> 10:04.930
Wait. Wait, Kazuki.

10:04.930 --> 10:07.880
I appreciate you getting angry on our behalf,

10:07.880 --> 10:10.010
but there's no point in starting a fight.

10:10.410 --> 10:11.180
Right?

10:23.800 --> 10:29.230
I promise to find a way to send 
you back in the near future.

10:29.230 --> 10:32.680
Until then, will you help us,

10:32.960 --> 10:34.650
heroes?

10:40.010 --> 10:43.700
Your Majesty, may I ask you a question?

10:43.700 --> 10:44.990
Of course.

10:45.620 --> 10:48.100
Why do you call us heroes?

10:48.100 --> 10:52.010
You know nothing about us.

10:52.800 --> 10:54.410
Because...

10:54.410 --> 10:55.750
Welcie.

10:55.750 --> 10:56.480
Yes, Your Majesty.

10:57.060 --> 11:02.990
The Hero Summoning's magic circle is 
designed to select accomplished individuals.

11:03.630 --> 11:07.290
I believe you heard bells ringing 
when you were summoned.

11:07.290 --> 11:09.720
That indicates that you are heroes.

11:11.000 --> 11:13.350
I see. That sound...

11:13.350 --> 11:14.110
Huh?

11:14.390 --> 11:16.510
But I thought Usato...

11:16.510 --> 11:19.900
Yeah, I didn't hear anything.

11:19.900 --> 11:26.550
Wait, does that mean... I just 
happened to get dragged into this?

11:28.370 --> 11:31.670
Mr. Kazuki, Ms. Suzune, and Mr. Usato.

11:31.670 --> 11:35.180
I'd like to use this crystal ball 
to measure your magical abilities.

11:35.800 --> 11:37.350
Wow.

11:37.350 --> 11:39.790
You can measure that with a crystal ball?

11:39.790 --> 11:42.310
Yes. I'll prepare it right away.

11:42.710 --> 11:45.710
Are you sure you're okay with this, Usato?

11:45.710 --> 11:49.810
Ms. Welcie said I might be able to use 
magic even though I'm not a hero.

11:50.170 --> 11:53.480
I appreciate them treating me 
the same as you two.

11:53.480 --> 11:54.890
That's not what I meant.

11:54.890 --> 11:57.360
Not only were you forced to come here,

11:57.360 --> 11:59.700
but you were also merely 
caught up in the summoning.

11:59.700 --> 12:02.530
Shouldn't you be angry about that?

12:02.530 --> 12:03.810
Oh, right.

12:03.810 --> 12:06.020
Getting angry about it won't help anything.

12:06.020 --> 12:09.670
I figure I might as well 
find something I can do.

12:11.830 --> 12:13.950
You're amazing.

12:13.950 --> 12:15.150
Am I?

12:15.150 --> 12:17.870
I'm pretty sure Inukami-senpai 
is way more amazing than me.

12:17.870 --> 12:18.890
She's so positive.

12:18.890 --> 12:21.280
I suppose you're right.

12:21.280 --> 12:24.310
Ms. Welcie, are you ready yet?

12:24.310 --> 12:26.870
We should try to be more positive, like her.

12:26.870 --> 12:31.450
<i>I don't think that's just positivity, 
but he doesn't need to know that.</i>

12:36.570 --> 12:39.160
Place your hands on the ball, Ms. Suzune.

12:39.410 --> 12:40.810
Here we go!

12:46.510 --> 12:47.830
It changed.

12:49.490 --> 12:53.600
This color indicates an 
affinity for thunder magic.

12:53.600 --> 12:56.420
You have ample mana, too. Incredible.

12:56.420 --> 12:57.610
Thunder...

12:58.490 --> 13:00.400
She seems happy.

13:00.400 --> 13:03.970
<i>Thunder magic tickles 
the edgelord in all of us.</i>

13:03.970 --> 13:06.100
Mr. Kazuki, go ahead.

13:06.420 --> 13:07.300
All right.

13:12.770 --> 13:15.250
This is the color of light magic.

13:15.250 --> 13:17.970
Light? What's that for?

13:17.970 --> 13:19.680
Blinding enemies?

13:19.680 --> 13:22.370
You use it to launch 
laser beams, Kazuki-kun.

13:22.370 --> 13:24.500
Or swords made of light.

13:24.500 --> 13:25.300
What?

13:25.300 --> 13:28.490
Senpai, Kazuki has no idea 
what you're talking about.

13:28.790 --> 13:32.360
You've got a sharp tongue, Usato-kun.

13:32.790 --> 13:35.030
I don't mind that, actually.

13:35.030 --> 13:39.890
<i>My perfect image of her has already 
shattered into a million pieces!</i>

13:39.890 --> 13:42.270
Light magic is incredible.

13:42.270 --> 13:44.800
Very few people can use it.

13:44.800 --> 13:46.970
Light dispels evil—

13:46.970 --> 13:50.770
Against demons, its power is unparalleled.

13:50.770 --> 13:52.740
I-It is?

13:52.740 --> 13:53.470
Yes.

13:53.470 --> 13:56.300
Mr. Usato, you're next. 
Place your hands on the ball.

13:56.300 --> 13:57.890
R-Right.

14:01.460 --> 14:04.880
<i>I wonder if I have any magical power.</i>

14:05.340 --> 14:10.570
<i>If I do, I hope I can use it 
to help Senpai and Kazuki.</i>

14:15.280 --> 14:18.070
It's pretty, like an emerald.

14:18.450 --> 14:21.050
Yes. It's a soothing color.

14:21.480 --> 14:24.390
Ms. Welcie, what kind of 
magical energy is this?

14:28.250 --> 14:30.410
I-I must tell him.

14:30.410 --> 14:31.340
Huh?

14:31.980 --> 14:34.570
I must tell him!

14:33.600 --> 14:34.800
Ms. Welcie?

14:34.800 --> 14:36.970
You two stay here, please!

14:35.300 --> 14:36.960
Ms. Welcie! Ms. Welcie!

14:37.460 --> 14:39.650
Couldn't you just beat me instead?!

14:41.150 --> 14:42.300
Your Majesty!

14:42.580 --> 14:44.270
Ah, Welcie.

14:44.270 --> 14:47.190
Have you determined Suzune 
and Kazuki's magical abilities?

14:47.190 --> 14:49.970
They both possess incredible abilities.

14:50.360 --> 14:52.860
But more importantly, Mr. Usato...

14:52.860 --> 14:54.740
What about him?

14:54.740 --> 14:58.830
Don't tell me he has an 
affinity for dark magic.

15:00.290 --> 15:01.950
The crystal ball turned green.

15:02.660 --> 15:04.660
What? Are you certain?!

15:04.660 --> 15:08.830
Yes. In other words, Mr. Usato has an 
affinity for the extraordinarily rare—

15:08.830 --> 15:11.030
Don't say it!

15:11.030 --> 15:14.150
<i>What? Is my magical 
affinity really that bad?</i>

15:14.150 --> 15:17.470
We must send Usato away from the 
castle as quickly as possible.

15:17.470 --> 15:20.050
Where should he go? 
Where's the safest place for him?

15:20.050 --> 15:22.560
F-For now, shouldn't we send him into town?

15:22.560 --> 15:23.720
Y-You're right.

15:24.020 --> 15:25.640
Make the arrangements right away.

15:25.640 --> 15:28.530
I don't understand.

15:28.530 --> 15:31.570
Am I dangerous or something?

15:31.570 --> 15:34.500
Is there anyone else who 
 possesses the same affinity?

15:34.500 --> 15:37.910
Y-Yes, there is someone, but...

15:37.910 --> 15:40.820
Not her! For so many reasons, not her!

15:54.470 --> 15:55.690
This isn't good.

15:55.690 --> 15:58.100
Wh-Why did it have to be now?

16:01.060 --> 16:04.700
Your Majesty, how did 
the summoning ritual go?

16:04.700 --> 16:06.870
Have the heroes already arrived?

16:06.870 --> 16:10.640
R-Rose, I thought you took the day off.

16:11.020 --> 16:12.750
You must be joking.

16:12.750 --> 16:15.700
I serve the king. I would never...

16:21.490 --> 16:23.410
Are you a hero?

16:24.840 --> 16:27.010
H-He's not a hero.

16:27.010 --> 16:30.170
He's a boy brought here by our ineptitude.

16:30.170 --> 16:33.830
He's ordinary. He's an 
extremely ordinary boy.

16:39.530 --> 16:41.720
Is he, now?

16:42.160 --> 16:43.270
Hey, kid.

16:43.270 --> 16:43.940
Yes?

16:43.940 --> 16:45.550
What's your name?

16:45.550 --> 16:48.350
I-It's Usato.

16:48.650 --> 16:51.700
Usato, huh? I am Rose.

16:51.700 --> 16:55.530
I'm the captain of the kingdom's Rescue Team.

16:55.910 --> 16:57.210
Nice to meet you.

16:57.210 --> 16:58.970
Uh, sure.

16:58.970 --> 17:00.460
<i>Rescue Team?</i>

17:00.460 --> 17:05.110
<i>She seems like someone who 
takes lives, not saves them.</i>

17:05.110 --> 17:08.680
M-Ms. Rose, the heroes are 
in the crystal ball room.

17:08.680 --> 17:10.120
I'll show you the way.

17:10.120 --> 17:10.910
I see.

17:10.910 --> 17:13.250
Your Majesty, please excuse me.

17:15.040 --> 17:16.430
R-Right.

17:17.900 --> 17:21.260
Usato, I'll decide what 
to do with you later.

17:21.260 --> 17:24.470
I'll have a room prepared for you. 
You can rest there.

17:24.470 --> 17:28.350
Okay, but you still haven't 
told me about my magic.

17:28.350 --> 17:31.280
What kind of magic is that green color?

17:35.890 --> 17:38.650
Did you say green?

17:38.650 --> 17:40.580
What? Yes.

17:40.810 --> 17:43.990
Your Majesty, I'll be borrowing this boy.

17:43.990 --> 17:46.420
Welcie, get Usato away from her!

17:46.420 --> 17:47.700
Y-Yes, Your Majesty!

17:57.790 --> 17:58.670
Rose!

17:58.670 --> 18:00.090
Wait!

18:27.330 --> 18:28.740
Your Majesty!

18:30.260 --> 18:36.170
I shall turn this boy into a 
full-fledged healing magic user!

18:36.170 --> 18:38.260
Wait, Rose!

18:38.260 --> 18:41.590
I know you're looking for 
healing magic users!

18:41.590 --> 18:47.510
But Usato really was just dragged into this!

18:47.510 --> 18:49.630
What? He was taken away?

18:49.630 --> 18:52.940
What do you mean by that? Is Usato in danger?

18:52.940 --> 18:57.350
He's not going to be killed 
or anything like that.

18:57.730 --> 18:58.650
Then...

18:58.650 --> 19:03.280
Mr. Usato was taken to a place 
a short distance from here.

19:04.170 --> 19:08.070
To the Rescue Team beyond the castle town.

19:08.070 --> 19:09.520
The Rescue Team?

19:10.000 --> 19:14.080
The crystal ball indicated that Mr. Usato 
has an affinity for healing magic.

19:14.080 --> 19:17.870
Healing magic users themselves 
are incredibly rare.

19:17.870 --> 19:20.510
Ms. Rose is one of them.

19:20.510 --> 19:24.240
She intends to train 
Mr. Usato as her subordinate.

19:24.750 --> 19:28.310
That doesn't sound like a problem.

19:28.310 --> 19:31.070
I'm not sure how to put this.

19:32.350 --> 19:36.930
Ms. Rose's training methods 
are a bit unorthodox.

19:36.930 --> 19:41.290
The subordinates she produces are, well...

19:44.240 --> 19:45.100
What?

19:45.580 --> 19:47.540
I'm a healing magic user?

19:48.440 --> 19:49.700
Me?

19:49.710 --> 19:53.070
At the very least, you have 
the predisposition to be one.

19:53.070 --> 19:56.040
That's why I brought you 
to the Rescue Team.

19:56.040 --> 19:58.470
As of today, this is your home.

19:58.470 --> 19:59.340
Okay.

19:59.340 --> 20:01.000
Boys, get in here.

20:01.000 --> 20:02.160
Yes, boss!

20:02.920 --> 20:05.590
You called, boss?

20:05.880 --> 20:08.460
<i>They're terrifying!</i>

20:08.760 --> 20:11.490
This is Usato. As of today, 
we'll be looking after him.

20:11.490 --> 20:12.890
Play nice.

20:12.890 --> 20:14.680
Yes, boss!

20:18.610 --> 20:21.380
I'm Tong. Nice to meet you, newbie.

20:21.380 --> 20:23.660
I'm Mill. Nice to meet you, newbie.

20:23.660 --> 20:26.200
I'm Alec. Nice to meet you, newbie.

20:26.200 --> 20:28.200
I'm Gomul. Nice to meet you, newbie.

20:28.200 --> 20:30.600
I'm Gurd. Nice to meet you, newbie.

20:31.800 --> 20:33.770
I-I'm sorry!

20:33.770 --> 20:37.710
<i>Am I an offering? Is she 
sacrificing me to them?</i>

20:39.310 --> 20:40.550
Boys!

20:40.550 --> 20:43.180
Don't scare the new guy!

20:43.180 --> 20:46.920
Boss, this is just how we welcome someone!

20:46.920 --> 20:49.360
We're being super nice to him!

20:49.360 --> 20:52.300
<i>They are? I don't think 
they know what "nice" means!</i>

20:53.550 --> 20:57.820
These are my subordinates, 
but they're not healing magic users.

20:57.820 --> 21:01.740
There are two other healing magic 
users on the Rescue Team,

21:01.740 --> 21:03.990
but normally they work elsewhere.

21:03.990 --> 21:05.780
So...

21:05.780 --> 21:07.150
So?

21:07.150 --> 21:11.330
I'll drum into you how to use healing magic.

21:11.330 --> 21:13.810
<i>"Don't get involved with her."</i>

21:13.810 --> 21:16.500
<i>Every fiber of my being 
is telling me that!</i>

21:16.500 --> 21:19.340
If possible, I'd like to learn from another—

21:19.340 --> 21:20.900
Training starts tomorrow.

21:20.900 --> 21:21.920
Prepare yourself.

21:21.920 --> 21:24.910
<i>Has what </i>I<i> want just flown away, then?!</i>

21:24.910 --> 21:26.360
You can stay in...

21:26.360 --> 21:29.130
Tong, there's space in your room, right?

21:29.130 --> 21:30.860
Show him what to do.

21:30.860 --> 21:32.670
Yes, boss.

21:32.670 --> 21:35.360
Today, eat dinner and get some rest.

21:37.780 --> 21:39.500
You're screwed.

21:39.500 --> 21:41.990
The boss is training you herself.

21:41.990 --> 21:44.050
She's gonna put you through hell.

21:44.050 --> 21:46.440
Better hope hell is the worst 
thing that happens to you.

21:46.880 --> 21:48.370
<i>Aw, man.</i>

21:51.520 --> 21:54.940
<i>What's going to happen to me?</i>

21:57.230 --> 21:59.280
I'm sure it'll work out.

21:59.280 --> 22:00.370
I should sleep.

22:01.160 --> 22:04.620
A healing magic user 
from another world, huh?

22:07.050 --> 22:09.590
We'll see how that turns out.

22:24.530 --> 22:29.200
<b>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</b>
